Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:38:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FunKey S: the version picker (several games in FunKey/isaac)

With several versions of the game in FunKey/isaac (Isaac.exe, Isaac-Eternal.exe...), main.cpp asks which one to
play, as upstream's chooser does on a PC, but on the console's screen with its buttons and before the game is
loaded: in the FunKey menu's style on black, one version at a time in the box (its name in capitals, on two lines
when too wide) with "Press A to play", Up and Down sliding in the others (wrapping round, repeating when held), A
or Start plays it ("Loading..." until the game shows), Menu quits back to the launcher; a power-off meanwhile
powers off. The choice is kept in isaac.ini (game = og|wotl|eternal) and offered first the next time. Not for
test scripts. The screen and the buttons are opened by whichever comes first (ioOpen); the menu's drawing is
shared (boxDraw, menuBox, writePpm). Test hooks: ISAAC_FUNKEY_PICK_TEST=<names> (the picker with one game: the
answer is only logged), ISAAC_FUNKEY_PICK_SHOTS=<prefix> (its pictures, without waiting for a button).
